From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:01 2001
From: Trey Moen <trey@moen.ai>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 03:30:00 -0700
Subject: cam: icp: keep FW alive after boot and defuse its boot watchdog

The sdm845 ICP FW dies with SYS_ERROR SFR "ICP SS WD Timeout" a
constant ~0.7 s after its first boot on mainline unless it receives
host HFI traffic after SYS_INIT: verified by discriminator runs where
HFI messages every 200 ms kept the FW healthy indefinitely (and the
deadline never re-armed after traffic stopped), while an untouched
running FW, a hard-close power collapse and a PC_PREP-handshake power
collapse all died on the same deadline. Legacy 4.9 is immune because
its camerad flow talks to the FW immediately.

Keep the FW running after the boot-time download (skip the power
collapse - the WD state survives collapse and kills the resumed
instance) and send two benign NULL-user_data pings at +250/+500 ms
(the ping-ack handler tolerates a NULL context). Skip the acquire-time
resume re-init when the a5 is already powered so cpas_start is not
double-invoked.
---

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_icp/icp_hw/icp_hw_mgr/cam_icp_hw_mgr.c b/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_icp/icp_hw/icp_hw_mgr/cam_icp_hw_mgr.c
index ed38387..9bbb682 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_icp/icp_hw/icp_hw_mgr/cam_icp_hw_mgr.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/msm/camera/camera_kt/drivers/cam_icp/icp_hw/icp_hw_mgr/cam_icp_hw_mgr.c
@@ -3773,6 +3773,12 @@ static int cam_icp_mgr_icp_resume(struct cam_icp_hw_mgr *hw_mgr)
 		return rc;
 	}
 
+	if (((struct cam_hw_info *)icp_dev_intf->hw_priv)->hw_state ==
+		CAM_HW_STATE_POWER_UP) {
+		CAM_DBG(CAM_ICP, "ICP already powered, skip resume");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	rc = icp_dev_intf->hw_ops.init(icp_dev_intf->hw_priv, NULL, 0);
 	if (rc)
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -3856,8 +3862,22 @@ static int cam_icp_mgr_hw_open(void *hw_mgr_priv, void *download_fw_args)
 		return rc;
 
 	rc = cam_ipe_bps_deint(hw_mgr);
-	rc = cam_icp_mgr_icp_power_collapse(hw_mgr);
-	CAM_DBG(CAM_ICP, "deinit all clocks at boot up");
+
+	/*
+	 * Do not power collapse the ICP after the boot-time download on
+	 * sdm845: the FW (CICP.FW.1.0-00050) arms a subsystem watchdog at
+	 * boot that survives the collapsed state and kills the next
+	 * instance ~0.7 s after first boot ("SFR: ICP SS WD Timeout") in
+	 * every PC flavor tried (hard close, PC_PREP handshake). Keep the
+	 * FW running - it services its own WD once it has seen host
+	 * traffic after SYS_INIT - and send a benign ping (NULL user_data
+	 * is handled) to defuse the boot watchdog window.
+	 */
+	msleep(250);
+	hfi_send_system_cmd(HFI_CMD_SYS_PING, 0, 0);
+	msleep(250);
+	hfi_send_system_cmd(HFI_CMD_SYS_PING, 0, 0);
+	CAM_INFO(CAM_ICP, "FW kept alive after boot download (WD defused)");
 
 	return rc;
 
